From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: riehlies <118917105+riehlies@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Solver Settings: Parameter Tolerance and Initial Grid of
 the adaptive solve
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Proposed by kisi (riehlies/kisi, web/advanced/fork-patches/): the
quasi-static adaptive solve's parameter tolerance was fixed at 5 % in
solve_worker.js and its initial grid at 30 cells per axis in getParams; both
become settings – *Parameter Tolerance (%)* (default 5) and *Initial Grid
(cells per axis)* (default 30), in the Solver Settings and the link's
settings – so that a page that hands a cross-section over can ask for the
same adaptive mesh as its own solver (kisi: 1 % energy and parameter
tolerance, a 10-cell initial grid, 60 k nodes, one converged pass), and the
same geometry gives the same numbers.
---
 FORK.md                    | 5 +++--
 src/app_solver.js          | 7 +++++++
 src/field_solver.html      | 8 ++++++++
 src/solve_worker.js        | 4 ++--
 tests/fork/check_hooks.mjs | 2 +-
 5 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/FORK.md b/FORK.md
index 20b9997..3055c09 100644
--- a/FORK.md
+++ b/FORK.md
@@ -103,8 +103,9 @@ Further changes of the original's files, also marked `FORK`:
 
 | File | Change |
 |---|---|
-| `src/field_solver.html` | page metadata of the hosted version (canonical URL, author, description instead of the original's site and icons), notice of the modified version and license text in the About tab, input and help text *Trace Width (top)* |
-| `src/app_solver.js` | setting `bs_w_top` (default and settings table) |
+| `src/field_solver.html` | page metadata of the hosted version (canonical URL, author, description instead of the original's site and icons), notice of the modified version and license text in the About tab, input and help text *Trace Width (top)*, inputs *Parameter Tolerance (%)* and *Initial Grid (cells per axis)* in the Solver Settings |
+| `src/app_solver.js` | setting `bs_w_top` (default and settings table); settings `param_tolerance` and `initial_grid` (default, settings table, bounds; the initial grid replaces the fixed 30 cells per axis in `getParams`) |
+| `src/solve_worker.js` | the quasi-static adaptive solve takes `param_tolerance` (the original's fixed 5 % as the default) |
 | `src/solver_factory.js` | passes `trace_width_top` |
 | `src/broadside_stripline.js` | upper trace with its own width, domain margin and enclosure check with the wider trace |
 | `src/tri_solver/tri_backend.js` | mesh reference width: the narrower trace |
diff --git a/src/app_solver.js b/src/app_solver.js
index 1c7d28c..cbb010e 100644
--- a/src/app_solver.js
+++ b/src/app_solver.js
@@ -211,6 +211,8 @@ const DEFAULT_SETTINGS = {
     enclosure_height: NaN, // auto
     max_iters: 10,
     tolerance: 0.01,
+    param_tolerance: 0.05,  // FORK: parameter tolerance of the quasi-static adaptive solve
+    initial_grid: DEFAULT_GRID_N,  // FORK: initial grid of the adaptive solve (cells per axis)
     min_converged_passes: 2,
     estimate_error: 1,
     max_nodes: 20,
@@ -330,6 +332,8 @@ const SETTINGS_FIELDS = [
     ['enclosure_height', 'inp_enclosure_height', 'unit', 'sphl'],
